# Game logic purity (`src/game/`)

All modules under `src/game/` are **pure, seed-driven game logic**. Follow these rules on every edit:

## Forbidden

- React / DOM imports (`react`, `react-dom`, `document`, `window`)
- Gameplay `Math.random()` — use the seeded `Rng` class (`rng.ts`)
- `any` types
- Live `fetch` for gameplay (static bake JSON via `bakedPois.ts` / `playable.ts` is the allowed exception)

## Required patterns

- Functions take explicit params and return new values (immutable updates)
- Randomness: `rng.fork('subsystem:key')` so unrelated systems don't share sequence state
- New mechanics → new module `src/game/<system>.ts`, wire through `store.ts` / `advanceTime` — do not grow a second Zustand store

## Allowed exceptions

- `randomSeed()` in `rng.ts` may use `Math.random()` to mint a fresh run seed string
- Cosmetic flavour helpers (`combatFlavor.ts`, `flavor.ts`) may use `Math.random()`
- Score HTTP lives in `src/api/` and `worker/`, not here

## Example

```typescript
// BAD — non-deterministic combat
const roll = Math.floor(Math.random() * 20) + 1;

// GOOD — seeded fork per encounter
const combatRng = rng.fork(`combat:${locationId}:${round}`);
const roll = combatRng.d20();
```
